        <p>ALL LADIES will be glad to hear that Mrs. M. Damerau, CERTIFICATED MIDWIFE, has a safe and certain mixture for obstructions and irregularities, which she will send, post free, for 4s. 91. It is absolutely guaranteed, even in long-standing obstinate cases. It cannot fail, and is perfectly harmless. -Do not trust in bogus advertisements of quacks and other Ignorant people, they never send you the right remedy. If you have already done to, send for this Mixture as a last resource, and you will not he deceived. Yen will find that it is always cheaper to come to the right place first. Below are some testimonials received. The originals of these, with thousands of others, can be seen any time. From Mrs. Chethans : Madam, will you kindly, send again one bottle of your Female Mixture, as the last acted splendidly. I enclose &amp;c."—Mrs. Binnte writes "Kindly forward by return of at a bottle of your Female Mixture. It put me all right last oime' and I trust it will do so —From Mrs. Pleteltsr t "Madame, I received the Mixture all right, and I took the doses as stated; it did all that was needed, for which I thank you very much.r—Mrs. S. writes from Sheffield: "I am pleased to tell you your medicine did all that was required, though I thought it had failed, fOr. I had the last dose thirty hours before any change took place. I had the last dote on Sunday, and all was right as possible Tuesday afternoon. Everything had been as well as It was possible. Hal I written toyou at first, I should have been over £2 in pocket. You ntay sbow this letter, but cover name and addrees."—Mrt. Bryan writes: "Madam, I am glad to be able to report that to. • last two doses have had the desired effect. I shall recommend your remedy to all my married friends. I think it is excellent, and should I be in difficulty again myself, shouldat once apply to you," —From Mrs. Garside : "I have muc h pleasure in sending you news of haying relief the first morning, for which I Rin very thankful indeed. I shall always fee_ grateful for your Mixture, and ill need anything again, I will send to you." Address: HRS. DAMMIA.U, Milton Cottage, Forest Hill, London</p>
