        <p>"Western Telegraph," of January 1, 1898 - 'Few houses in Manchester occupied in the same line of business are better known or enjoy a larger share of patronage than that of Samuel Pitts, late of Gaythorn, now oflLondon-road, Manchester, the complete house shop, and office furnisher. It was in 1845 that the present proprietor Initiated the business, operations having been firs com- menced by him in Brook-street as a cabinet maker and dealer in office furniture. By his energy and ability the concern prospered, and more accommodation becoming necessary, a move was made to the late premises in Gaythorn about 26 years since. Samuel Pitts soon acquired a name for the 1 superior excellence of the goods he supplied, the vast range of selection offered to customers, and the house advanced with rapid strides into a foremost and leading position in the trade. Just recently the Corporation purchased the Gay- thorn premises for street improvement purposes. and Samuel Pitts had once again to find fresh fields and pastures new.' This time his choice tell upon th,: vast edifice until latterly !mown as norougli Buildings, situate 100 to 120, London-road, which he has now converted into what is often termed the largest and most convenient general fun:ldling establishment in Man- chester. 'the premises occupied are enormous in extent and attractive in appearance and are prominently and com- mandingly located. They comprise a magnificent frontagS ' of plate-glass windows, well stocked with high-class goods, I togetly'r with extens've showrooms nearly 300 feet brig on the ground floor, and offices ,tnd counting house. The first, second, and third floors are occupied by a number of stock and showrooms, and extended workshop accommodation is offered by the premises on the opposite side of London-road. The establishment throughout has been admirably arranged, and thoroughly and elegantly fitted up with every require- ment, including electzie light throughout, hydraulic pas- senger and luggage lift to all floors, for the effective display of the splendid selection of goods, which cannot be surpassed by those of any competitor, either in extent, variety, or general superiority. In soundness of material, good work- manship, and elegance and novelty of d‘sign the house has no successful rivals in Manchester. while prices will always be found of the most satisfactory character. The proprietor is thoroughly acquainted with every eligible source of supply and in addition to his own special make the establishment displays the choicest specimens, both new and second-hand, of other well-known manufacturers. Samuel Pitts is a thoroughly practical man, and his personal supervision is bestemed upon the business in its entirety, He is able, ener- getic, and courteous in his control, and all his dealings are marked by his methods of strict fairness and honesty. In conclusion, we should strangly advise all furnishing, whether In part or throughout, to pay this establishment a visit. The same civility and courtesy is extended to all, whether buying or not, and the firm's well-known straightforward, syste- matic methpd ensures all orders being satisfactorily exe- cuted. ITTS'S HOUSES OF FURNITURE at 154-, 22, 28k, 381, 50, 75,100, up to 1,500 guineas are still unrivalled. Full particulars and testimonials on application. Cash price quoted ; deferred payment by arrangement. Inspection Invited. P ITT S'S DINING-ROOM FURNITURE. Best selection; utmost value. Hundreds of suites new and second- hand.</p>
        <p>"iIDITTS'S DRAWING-ROOM FURNITURE. All leading 1 designs In every conctivable covering. Grandest dis- play ever seen. DITTS'S BEDROOM FURNITURE. Solid wood through- -1 out. All fashionable makes. Bedsteads, Mattresses, Bedding, ao.</p>
        <p>PITTS'S CARPETS and FLOOR COVERINGS. Grandest selection anywhere. All English make. Fitted free.</p>
        <p>PITTS'S PIANOS. Thoroughly reliable, new and second- hand, Grand and Cottage, splendid selectim, utmost value, satisfaction assured. Cash or deferred payment.</p>
        <p>111DITTS'S CYCLES, BASSINHTTBS, LAMPS, CHINA EARTHENWARE, PICTURES, ENGRAVINGS,.OUT- LIMY, &amp;c., &amp;c. Marvellous value.</p>
