      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1898-02-11_WidnesExaminer_art0061" n="art0061">
        <head>GREAT SANKEY.</head>
        <p>GREAT SANKEY.</p>
        <p>DEATH OF lain. HENRY BATE —Mr. Henry Bite, of The Willows, Great Sankey, pas3ed away at his tesidence early on M(mday morning. Mr.ilate Wag well known and respected in the neighbourtlo id, having for many years officiated as overseer for the Great Sankey pai6h. Be always took a great incerest in church matters, and his death is universally regretted. The deceased gwnreaue was interred at Greystone Cemetery at 3 p-m on Thurs- day, the Rev. E. S. Jackson (vicar) officiating. There was a large attendance of friends awl sympathisers.</p>
