      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1898-02-11_WidnesExaminer_art0067" n="art0067">
        <head>MAKE NO MISTAKE.</head>
        <p>MAKE NO MISTAKE.</p>
        <p>Many people mistake a false for a true economy. Good economy " take care of the Pence, letting the pounds take care of themselves ;" bad economy is " a penny wise and a pound foolish." True economy is care- ful to make the " stitch in time which saves nine;" false economy risks the loss of a valuable horse for want of a nail in a horse shoe, or the has of a fine ship for the want of a pennyworth of tar. In all matters of economy the test question should always be" Can I afford it ?" For instance, when suffering from any slight ailment, ask yourself : Can I afford to let this slight cough or little cough develoi into asthma, chronic bronchitis, or consumption ? Ca : afford to let this " out of aorta" feeling which ir sailer -em occasionally to settle into a confirmed melancholy? Can I afford to let my wife grow weaker day by day rider household burdens, or my child,who is new only a little delicee,run the risk of being obliged to succumb entirely,or can,t myself afford to run the risk of breaking down entirely, and giving up my work, all for want of a little precaution ? When you are told hat the excellent preparation known as Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, which is acknowledged to be the best tonic remedy ever discovered, would enable you to avoid all these dangers, the question should not be "Can I afford it ?" but •• Can I afford to he without it ?" In most cases common sense will tell you that you cloister afford to be without it,that you cannot afford to run the risk you are now running, while no valuable a remedy as Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is at hand. If your occupation is an unhehltby one, If you are ex- posed to the weather, or work long hours in close rooms; if your constitution is weakened, or your health under- mined ; or if you are in any way not " up to the mark," use Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters,The Vegetable Tonic. It never fails to strengthen the weakened system, to brace the nerves and fortify the constitution. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is purely vegetable, and certified by Analysts to be pure and harmless. It may bs safely taken by delicate ladies and children in all cases of weak mess. Many people after enjoying the good things of life,are subject to much after suffering from the inability of the Stomach to perform its duties. A timely use of Gwilym Evans' Quinine Biters would strengthen the digestive organs, and serve to remedy the evil. We have no sympathy with those people who always complain of being ill and miserable and out of sorts,when a course of Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters would soon set them right. Sold in bottles Es. 9d. and 4s. Eld. each, by all chemists and patent medicine venaors,or direct from the proprietors : The Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Com- pany Limited, Llanelly, South Wal,s, carriage free by parcel post. Beware of imitations. See the name of " Gwilym EvanS "on label, stamp, and bottle ; anu re- fuse any preparation offered as a substitute for it. GWILVM TAVANS' QUININE BITTERS.</p>
