        <p>SCALDING FATALITY AT .WARRINGTON. An inquest was held in the Warrington Police Court on Tuesday afternoon by Mr. F. A. Jones, touching the death of Harold Stockton who died on Friday. James Stockton, 7, Brackley-street, father of deceased, said that the latter was aged 2 years. Witness saw him a quarter of an hour before the accident and after. He died on Friday morning. Jane Rosbottom, grandmother of the child, said that on the morning in ..question she was washing Clothes in the scullery and had a mug of boiling water on the floor. Deceased knocked the mug over and upset the boiling water on himself. Re was scalded on the left leg, and she put oil on and sent for Dr. M'Carthy.—A verdict of " accidental death," was returned. A BREAK-DOWN AT BANK QUAY. On Saturday morning between 11 o'clock and 12 o'clock, a goods train from Carlisle caused a block on the main line ju,t beyond Bank Quay station. it seems that a large bale of carpets fell from one of the waggons, and getting under the wheels threw five waggons off the line, their contents being strewn in all directions. A break-down gang was at once on the spot and working with great energy succeeded in getting the line cleared of debris be- fore 9 p.m. In the meantime the traffic from the North had to use the old line which runs below the embankment, and by this means much delay and Inconvenience were saved.</p>
