        <p>CHESHIRE LEN E:". —WATERLOO COURSING- MEETING. On WEDNI:SDAY, THURSDAY, and FRIDAY, FEBRUARY 16TH. 17ra and 182 a, 1893. SPECIAL EXPRESS TRAINS Will be run to MYNAH and HILLHOUSE (near the Course) as under : * Should the meet be at Lydiate on any of the days, the 'trams will run to and from Lydiate Station. TIMES. Wednesday Fares there and Stations. and Thursday Friday. back same day. a.m, am. am. lst cl. 3rd cl. Warrington (Central) dep. 9-25 11-0 8-55 Altair and Hillhouse arr. 10-0 11-45 9-30 4e. 25. The Speeial trains will return from Altcar and Hillhouse about half an hour after the Coursing is finished each day. 'Passengers can also return by any ordinary train. Should the Coursing be postponed the special Trains will not be run. For cheap bookings from Widnes. Farnworth, see Bills at the Stations. DAVID MELDRUM, Manager. Central Station, Liverpool. February. 1898. URBAN DISTRICT COUNCIL OF NEWTON-li= MARRIIFIELD.—TRNDRRS ARE INVITED for constructing sewers in the following streets, viz. : ATHOL-STREET ALBION-STREET CLARENCE STREET In accordance with plans and specifications which may be Inspected at my office. Tenders endorsed " Sewers " must be addressed to me and delivered at my ofKe not later than 10 a.m. on MONDAY. the 21st INSTANT. The lowest, or any tender will not necessarily be accepted. RICHARD BRIERLEY, Engineer and Surveyor to the Council. Town Hall. Earlestown. February 11th, 1898. STOCKTON HEATH PARISH COUNCIL —ASKS- TANT OVERSEER AND CLE.;K TO THE COUNCIL. The Council will be glad to RECEIVE APPLICATIONS for the APPOINTMENT of ASSISTANT OVERSEER and CLERK to the Council, salary about £4O per annum. Applications endorsed "Assistant Overseer," to be delivered to one not later than SATURDAY, the 19th inst. Canvassing members will be a disqualification. FREDERICK PEARSON, Ch drman of the Council. Springfield, Stockton Heath.</p>
